WEBVTT

00:41.916 --> 00:46.004
MY ROYAL NEMESIS

00:46.087 --> 00:47.172
CLOSED TODAY

00:56.639 --> 00:58.516
Boss, is that a woman right there?

00:59.017 --> 01:03.188
I can see just fine. Drag her out. Raze
everything to the ground!

01:03.772 --> 01:04.939
-Yes, boss!
-Yes, boss!

01:06.566 --> 01:07.400
-What the hell?
-Huh?

01:07.484 --> 01:08.318
What's going on?

01:15.825 --> 01:17.035
Who the hell are you?

01:18.870 --> 01:20.622
I'm Cha Se-gye, I'm in charge of Chail.

01:20.705 --> 01:22.082
I don't know you, should I?

01:22.874 --> 01:24.876
-Hey! Come on! Hey!
-Get him! Get him!

01:25.376 --> 01:27.337
-Hey!
-You're not goi--

01:27.420 --> 01:29.339
-Get him, damn it!
-Hey! Stop him!

01:30.298 --> 01:31.299
Hey, come on!

01:32.258 --> 01:33.551
Get him already! Come on!

01:35.428 --> 01:36.930
Oh! Whoa, whoa, whoa!

01:40.642 --> 01:42.769
Stop now! Police! Cease all operations.

01:46.606 --> 01:47.565
-Shin Seo-ri.
-Hey!

01:48.817 --> 01:49.651
Are you okay?

01:52.112 --> 01:53.822
-Cha Se-gye.
-Yeah.

01:54.614 --> 01:55.573
What is it?

01:58.701 --> 01:59.619
It's too bright.

02:01.287 --> 02:02.372
It's hurting my eyes.

02:07.210 --> 02:08.044
Shin Seo-ri.

02:11.881 --> 02:12.715
Shin Seo-ri.

02:20.140 --> 02:26.980
EPISODE 13
TWIST OF FATE

03:21.743 --> 03:24.704
-What's going on? Is she all right?
-I think she needs assistance. She really

03:24.787 --> 03:25.622
I don't know, I just saw her on the
ground, it's--

03:25.705 --> 03:29.167
-Has she been there for a long time?
-doesn't look well. Someone must

03:29.250 --> 03:31.169
-Dan-sim, can you hear me?
-come help.

03:31.252 --> 03:33.671
-Oh. She's opening her eyes,
-Are you all right?

03:33.755 --> 03:34.589
Dan-sim!

03:34.672 --> 03:36.758
My name is Seo-ri. Why is she…

04:08.581 --> 04:11.709
Your breathing has stabilized
considerably, and your overall numbers

04:11.793 --> 04:15.255
look fine, sir. As long as there are no
secondary infections or rebleeding,

04:15.338 --> 04:17.507
you should be discharged the week
after next.

04:17.590 --> 04:21.302
Sir, I don't know anything about it.
I have nothing to do with Mr. Cha's

04:21.386 --> 04:24.847
company or your accident. My only
intention was to work with Mr. Choi

04:24.931 --> 04:27.392
for mutual benefit. That's it.

04:27.892 --> 04:31.271
And if you continue to keep your mind
completely at rest, your memory should

04:31.354 --> 04:32.397
gradually recover too.

04:32.480 --> 04:35.024
I see, thank you. I will keep that
in mind.

04:41.406 --> 04:44.951
Contact the Commissioner General and
tell him that I want to see him.

05:00.883 --> 05:01.718
Are you okay?

05:02.927 --> 05:03.761
What?

05:04.929 --> 05:07.890
I just want to know if you're okay.

05:12.186 --> 05:15.273
You're like a ghost. Nothing gets
past you.

05:22.280 --> 05:23.406
What can I do?

05:25.742 --> 05:32.040
I'm not able to turn back time. It's no
good getting angry or crying over it.

05:34.959 --> 05:40.381
I have to focus on the present
and just do whatever I can.

05:41.174 --> 05:43.843
What is it? Has something happened?

05:45.928 --> 05:46.763
Cha Se-gye.

05:50.933 --> 05:57.857
I've always felt, all this time, life was
a punishment for me.

06:01.277 --> 06:02.487
Each day I…

06:04.989 --> 06:06.824
I felt I was being punished.

06:09.452 --> 06:12.413
That pigheaded child. I can't believe she
threw herself into the river.

06:12.497 --> 06:14.540
That wretch has no fear. Darn it.

06:14.624 --> 06:17.335
We have already signed her away into
slavery, but her senses have taken

06:17.418 --> 06:21.005
leave of her and she doesn't even
know her own name. What are we to do?

06:21.089 --> 06:23.758
What do you mean, what are we to do?
She can be a slave if she doesn't

06:23.841 --> 06:26.427
know her name. Send her off as soon as
she gets up!

06:28.179 --> 06:29.013
For goodness sake.

06:29.097 --> 06:32.809
Why had I ever been born if the
only thing awaiting me was punishment?

06:32.892 --> 06:36.312
Ugh, the miserable face on that girl
is getting on my nerves. If you

06:36.396 --> 06:39.232
keep that up after you're sold off, you
won't last long.

06:40.608 --> 06:43.027
Hey, hey, where are you going? Damn, you
wretch!

06:44.070 --> 06:47.407
Hey! Lock her in the shed and don't
give her a drop of water.

06:52.328 --> 06:55.081
If that was how my life was going to be,
I'd rather…

06:55.164 --> 06:57.625
Open this! Open it!

07:02.130 --> 07:04.215
The lowly wretch is soon to meet her end.

07:05.591 --> 07:08.970
Ugh, these are the end times indeed.
How dare that lowly wench do something

07:09.053 --> 07:09.887
like that?

07:12.640 --> 07:13.850
I'd rather…

07:14.475 --> 07:18.813
Who knows? It could be black magic
to bring about the Queen's death.

07:19.313 --> 07:21.357
SACRED SITE OF
THE ILLUSTRIOUS GRAND PRINCE CHEONGHEON

07:21.441 --> 07:23.943
Not have been born at all.

07:31.325 --> 07:35.037
Even when I landed here, although I told
myself I'd consider it a gift and

07:35.121 --> 07:40.042
make it out to be something of a… a
second chance of sorts,

07:42.712 --> 07:44.672
It still felt like another punishment.

07:46.757 --> 07:50.636
I wondered what kind of suffering
this life would bring.

07:58.060 --> 08:01.522
But do you know what's interesting?
I think I've smiled a little more

08:01.606 --> 08:03.608
since coming here.

08:05.818 --> 08:09.780
Since meeting grandma and since meeting
you my mind's been put at ease a little

08:09.864 --> 08:13.493
for the first time in my life.

08:20.875 --> 08:24.003
So I've decided to call it even.
I'm going to think of it as a

08:24.086 --> 08:27.715
reward. I'm going to think of it
as getting all the rewards I missed out

08:27.798 --> 08:29.675
on all at once.

08:52.365 --> 08:53.199
Cha Se-gye,

08:55.743 --> 08:57.828
let's never part and grow old together.

09:01.749 --> 09:02.833
I won't let you go.

09:07.004 --> 09:08.422
I won't let you go anywhere.

09:13.469 --> 09:19.976
Se-gye, I'm the one who's not going.
There's no reason to go back now.

09:22.645 --> 09:23.688
Because I'm exactly…

09:26.023 --> 09:26.983
where I should be.

09:33.614 --> 09:37.076
She had a high fever overnight, but
we administered some antipyretics

09:37.159 --> 09:41.205
and she's much better now. Even so, the
wind is cold, so try to go in soon.

09:44.834 --> 09:45.710
Grandma.

09:48.879 --> 09:50.047
It's your grandaughter.

10:05.771 --> 10:07.523
It's me. Your grandaughter is here.

10:11.193 --> 10:12.778
Won't you look at me, at least?

10:15.489 --> 10:16.324
Young lady.

10:21.370 --> 10:25.625
This man right here, is he… is he your
boyfriend?

10:28.794 --> 10:30.129
Yes, I am her boyfriend.

10:30.630 --> 10:33.341
What a tall and handsome young man,
just like my husband. He wasn't

10:33.424 --> 10:40.056
much good at making money, although he
really had a lovely face.

10:40.139 --> 10:43.309
I'm good at earning money as well, ma'am.
As I said last time,

10:43.392 --> 10:45.061
I'm a successful business man.

10:45.144 --> 10:47.688
This boy sure knows how to talk the talk.

10:55.738 --> 10:58.324
Pretty confident for a man who's lost
everything.

11:04.080 --> 11:05.289
Young lady, who are you?

11:08.793 --> 11:10.878
Why are you being so good to me?

11:16.342 --> 11:20.096
What do you mean? I'm his girlfriend.

11:51.961 --> 11:52.962
Don't cry.

11:55.172 --> 11:56.006
It's okay.

12:01.679 --> 12:05.099
What was all that yesterday? Telling me
to come there out of nowhere.

12:05.182 --> 12:07.643
No other option. They came without
warning. It shook me up too.

12:07.727 --> 12:10.563
Well, you should've kept me in the loop.
Same with your backroom deal with

12:10.646 --> 12:13.357
-Inspector Lee.
-How dare you call it a backroom deal?

12:14.024 --> 12:15.234
Make a deal with me.

12:15.317 --> 12:17.778
Don't tell me you're trying to
make a plea deal with an active

12:17.862 --> 12:19.947
duty police officer?

12:20.030 --> 12:22.867
Just sharing info. From what I've seen,
the cartel inside the police force

12:22.950 --> 12:24.869
runs as deep as sweet potato vines.

12:26.704 --> 12:29.665
When it comes to guerrilla-style combat,
timing's key. Gotta strike while the

12:29.749 --> 12:32.376
iron's hot. And speaking of timing,
I need you to work off site. Keep

12:32.460 --> 12:37.673
an eye on yesterday's restaurant.
Don't know when they'll come back.

12:37.757 --> 12:40.342
It'll be good for her to get some
fresh air rather than just staying

12:40.426 --> 12:41.427
in her room all day.

12:42.636 --> 12:44.597
Could I have a word with you, Ms. Shin?

12:55.191 --> 12:58.068
We just wanted to let you know that
her meds are gonna be…

12:58.152 --> 13:00.488
You have high standards, young man.
Very high.

13:02.156 --> 13:03.824
You sure have picked a good one.

13:04.825 --> 13:05.826
What are you saying?

13:11.707 --> 13:14.710
How do you know when you pretty much just
met her right now?

13:16.504 --> 13:19.089
Just met her right now? She's my child
that I raised with my own two

13:19.173 --> 13:25.888
hands. Hey, there is something I'd
really like to say.

13:26.889 --> 13:28.891
Oh, okay, just wait here. I'll go get her
right--

13:28.974 --> 13:29.809
No.

13:31.060 --> 13:35.314
Not Seo-ri, you. I have something I
want to say to you.

13:45.324 --> 13:49.161
So, it wasn't a spirit possession, but a
reclamation? Not a forced occupation,

13:49.245 --> 13:51.121
just a triumphant return?

13:54.583 --> 13:58.254
At just 12, you landed in Joseon
and lived as a court lady until you were

13:58.337 --> 14:01.715
executed by poison, at which point
you returned to the present day.

14:01.799 --> 14:06.887
I've never come across a case like
this one before.

14:09.098 --> 14:12.810
It's essentially like discovering
a whole new continent. Oh, now I get it.

14:12.893 --> 14:16.313
That's why I thought that transcendent
vision I had was odd. She had

14:16.397 --> 14:20.526
your looks, but it didn't seem like she
was you.

14:20.609 --> 14:21.652
Must've been the girl.

14:21.735 --> 14:25.531
Anyway, the conclusion I've come to
is that I never have to experience a

14:25.614 --> 14:28.868
transcendent vision ever again nor be
possessed by a spirit.

14:34.582 --> 14:36.083
Congratulations, Your Highness.

14:36.166 --> 14:37.585
No, no, no.

14:38.210 --> 14:41.547
Do not address me as "Your Highness"
anymore. I'm Seo-ri, alright?

14:41.630 --> 14:43.799
Shin Seo-ri. That's my name now.

14:44.717 --> 14:50.848
A-ha. Shin Seo-ri? Oh, yes. This really
is the start of a new life for you.

14:50.931 --> 14:53.100
If I am to make a proper fresh
start, I need to prune the

14:53.183 --> 14:55.436
rotten branches and get some things in
order.

14:58.105 --> 15:00.816
His Majesty the King has issued
his decree. Huibin Kim, you have

15:00.900 --> 15:04.111
committed the most heinous crime of
disrupting the order of the royal court,

15:04.194 --> 15:06.572
and as such, you shall be put to death
by poison.

15:06.655 --> 15:10.868
Is it a crime for one to have loved His
Majesty? I must see the King. Allow me a

15:10.951 --> 15:12.620
proper audience with him.

15:13.120 --> 15:14.330
Force it down.

15:17.791 --> 15:21.921
You wenches! You unhand me this instant!
Bring His Majesty here!

15:22.463 --> 15:23.714
Bring him here at once.

15:24.673 --> 15:26.216
I shall not perish like this.

15:28.969 --> 15:29.803
Bring it in!

15:35.017 --> 15:38.395
So you are truly determined to kill me
and rid yourself of me? Very

15:38.479 --> 15:42.399
well. Let us die together today.

15:51.533 --> 15:53.953
I will have my revenge.

15:55.829 --> 15:58.999
Wow, you totally killed the poison
drinking scene. The dopeamine

15:59.083 --> 16:01.835
hit is unreal. It feels like you've
experienced that.

16:02.336 --> 16:07.007
Practice makes perfect, they always say.
It's thanks to me if rating soar.

16:07.716 --> 16:11.470
Noona, the director said he should bring
you back in season three as the twin,

16:11.553 --> 16:13.055
with just a mole on your nose.

16:14.640 --> 16:18.519
Dying young really creeps me out though.
Next time, I'm living to an old age.

16:21.146 --> 16:24.608
Makeup team. Could you wipe the blood off
Seo-ri's lips please?

16:26.026 --> 16:27.653
Look at you, all excited, Shin Seo-ri.

16:27.736 --> 16:29.947
Hey, you. Bring me some water.

16:30.948 --> 16:31.782
Oh. Oh, gosh.

16:36.370 --> 16:37.204
I appreciate it.

16:39.540 --> 16:41.917
Where's the wrap party for Seo-ri's
last shoot?

16:43.293 --> 16:44.128
Wrap party?

16:45.170 --> 16:46.547
Haven't you been invited?

16:47.715 --> 16:48.590
Oh, uh…

16:49.675 --> 16:53.512
Whoa, no way. After looking out for you,
she's suddenly decided she doesn't like

16:53.595 --> 16:54.430
you anymore?

16:55.347 --> 16:57.474
Wait, what do you mean looking out
for me?

16:58.642 --> 17:02.229
You don't know? She's the one who got
you your role. It didn't take her

17:02.312 --> 17:05.482
long to flip after overstepping
when she was a substitute hire.

17:05.566 --> 17:09.194
Shows how fickle she is. Who does
she think she is anyway, to tell me to

17:09.278 --> 17:12.114
come to her wrap party?

17:22.833 --> 17:25.627
Apparently, she's a family member
of the nurse. Security's been trying to

17:25.711 --> 17:27.212
force her out, but they can't.

17:27.296 --> 17:29.631
DEATH OF NURSE AN SEONG-HUI
I DEMAND THE TRUTH

17:30.299 --> 17:32.718
Why is she here rather than at Biojei?

17:32.801 --> 17:35.054
It must've been Cha that leaked the info
to her.

17:35.137 --> 17:36.221
Get rid of her…

17:37.556 --> 17:38.891
before the word gets out.

17:40.225 --> 17:41.060
Yes, sir.

17:49.693 --> 17:51.904
Yeah, but she never would've said that
had you been there.

17:51.987 --> 17:53.864
Is he still coming or is he gonna bail?

17:53.947 --> 17:56.909
-You did a great job. Seriously.
-You really did a great job. Gosh. It was

17:56.992 --> 18:00.370
-You really did a great job.
-honestly good. This is so delicious.

18:00.454 --> 18:02.831
-We need a toast. Seo-ri, make a toast.
-Go on.

18:03.665 --> 18:07.503
All right, guys. Thank you for coming
to celebrate my completion of filming.

18:07.586 --> 18:11.215
In all of your personal lives, and in
your work lives, I wish you health

18:11.298 --> 18:16.970
and longevity, and great success. Now,
everyone, say, "Muyaho!"

18:17.846 --> 18:19.515
-Muyaho?
-What?

18:19.598 --> 18:20.516
-M-- muyaho?
-What?

18:20.599 --> 18:22.267
-Uh…
-Muyaho?

18:22.351 --> 18:23.185
Muyaho?

18:23.852 --> 18:24.728
Muyaho!

18:25.270 --> 18:26.605
Oh, muyaho!

18:26.688 --> 18:27.898
Yeah, muyaho!

18:27.981 --> 18:29.399
Yeah, that's right!

18:30.359 --> 18:31.568
Cheers! Cheers.

18:31.652 --> 18:32.820
Hell yeah!

18:32.903 --> 18:33.737
Cheers.

18:36.198 --> 18:37.407
Wow, that is so--

18:40.202 --> 18:43.122
What are you all doing here? Are you
friends with Seo-ri?

18:43.205 --> 18:46.166
Well, Gwang-nam kept asking us to come,
so honestly, it was kinda hard to keep

18:46.250 --> 18:48.335
turning him down.

18:54.007 --> 18:57.219
Right. I'm sure that's all it is.

18:57.302 --> 19:00.430
Eat and drink up, everyone. Boss man's
got this.

19:00.514 --> 19:06.770
Hey. Gwang-nam, quit getting drinks for
everyone else and drink with us.

19:06.854 --> 19:07.855
Hey, yeah.

19:07.938 --> 19:08.772
Let's do a cheers.

19:08.856 --> 19:11.316
I gotta drive tonight, so you guys
drink my share for me.

19:11.400 --> 19:13.360
Oh, wow. You're so nice.

19:13.861 --> 19:16.822
What's with your voice? I really
love your voice.

19:16.905 --> 19:17.739
My voice?

19:18.991 --> 19:20.159
Let's toast with water.

19:20.242 --> 19:21.577
-Come on. Cheers.
-Cheers.

19:21.660 --> 19:22.995
-Cheers.
-Cheers.

19:24.538 --> 19:25.873
Dude, seriously?

19:32.713 --> 19:34.840
No. Not as much as he's had, not at all.

19:35.340 --> 19:38.385
-Huh? What's this? What's this? Wait,
-What are they bringing in? Hey, what's

19:38.468 --> 19:39.511
-what's going on?
-the deal?

19:39.595 --> 19:40.512
Wow, this is nuts.

19:40.596 --> 19:43.223
-Is it for us? Gift bags, no way.
-Dang, for everyone, or…

19:43.307 --> 19:45.559
-Huh?
-Here you all are.

19:45.642 --> 19:46.643
Cha Se-gye.

19:50.022 --> 19:52.024
What're you doing at my wrap party?

19:52.107 --> 19:55.527
I heard Biojei's brand ambassador,
Seo-ri, has just finished her last shoot

19:55.611 --> 19:58.071
today, so I prepared gift bags for the
film crew.

19:58.739 --> 19:59.573
Oh…

20:00.949 --> 20:05.162
First of all, the Dynaestie Premium
three-piece set for your beauty. A Chail

20:05.245 --> 20:07.414
-Conic Bluetooth speaker.
-Nice!

20:08.165 --> 20:10.209
Oh, dang. That's amazing!

20:10.751 --> 20:14.504
The full Chail Tech set comprising watch,
tablet, and also a headset.

20:16.256 --> 20:17.174
I can't believe it.

20:17.257 --> 20:20.510
-Shin Seo-ri! Shin Seo-ri! Shin Seo-ri!
-Shin Seo-ri! Shin Seo-ri! Shin Seo-ri!

20:20.594 --> 20:22.095
-Shin Seo-ri!
-Shin Seo-ri! Shin Seo-ri!

20:22.179 --> 20:23.180
Shin Seo-ri! Here they come

20:23.263 --> 20:25.265
Shin Seo-ri!
This is so great.

20:26.475 --> 20:27.559
Shin Seo-ri!

20:28.518 --> 20:30.520
-Shin Seo-ri! Shin Seo-ri!
-Shin Seo-ri! Shin Seo-ri!

20:30.604 --> 20:31.688
Really, it's nothing.

20:35.943 --> 20:38.445
Are you trying to bankrupt yourself?
Why are you throwing all this

20:38.528 --> 20:39.363
money around?

20:39.446 --> 20:42.032
I'm investing, that's all. This
industry's a small world. Could run

20:42.115 --> 20:44.785
into these people again. That's why
you invest in stuff that will gain

20:44.868 --> 20:45.786
compound interest.

20:46.912 --> 20:50.874
Compound interest? You should worry about
yourself instead of spending your money.

20:50.958 --> 20:53.377
When are you going to stop living so
carelessly?

20:54.503 --> 20:58.257
What's this, Shin Seo-ri? Do you worry
about me day and night? I'll be busy

20:58.340 --> 21:02.010
so we won't see each other. How will you
handle that?

21:11.937 --> 21:14.439
Why do I keep seeing couples everywhere?

21:16.316 --> 21:17.192
-Gwang-nam.
-Yes.

21:17.276 --> 21:20.445
How long are you planning to work as
Shin Seo-ri's manager? Don't your

21:20.529 --> 21:21.863
parents say anything?

21:21.947 --> 21:24.324
They have been nagging me to move
home, actually. But I really

21:24.408 --> 21:26.702
don't want to live in the countryside.

21:26.785 --> 21:28.078
What's wrong with that?

21:28.662 --> 21:31.873
Living in the countryside is my dream.
Kinfolk style.

21:32.374 --> 21:33.417
"Kinfolk."

21:34.501 --> 21:36.962
Kinfolk, my ass. Didn't you say
everywhere outside of Gangnam was

21:37.045 --> 21:40.007
just a rural dump? And that you could
never live anywhere lower than the 20th

21:40.090 --> 21:40.924
floor?

21:43.302 --> 21:44.803
When did I say that?

21:45.304 --> 21:49.516
Well, I only meant that the air
quality is bad in Seoul on lower floors.

21:49.599 --> 21:51.226
Yeah, I have heard that as well.

21:51.727 --> 21:52.894
I live on the second floor of a

21:52.978 --> 21:55.314
-boarding house, and if someone smokes
-Oh. Really?

21:55.397 --> 21:58.191
A cigarette outside, there's literally no
escaping it. And the room is so

21:58.275 --> 22:00.444
-Wh--
-small that the smell lingers forever.

22:00.527 --> 22:03.780
-It's the worst.
-Oh, you live in a boarding house? Why?

22:04.906 --> 22:09.286
Why? Uh… 'Cause I'm, um… I don't have a
deposit?

22:09.786 --> 22:12.831
So why in the world don't you have a
deposit? Oh, are your parents doing that

22:12.914 --> 22:16.460
on purpose to teach you independence?

22:16.543 --> 22:17.502
Independence?

22:18.628 --> 22:22.299
Oh, nah, nah. Oh, no. My parents used to
always have about five million won

22:22.382 --> 22:25.927
on hand, it's just they got scammed last
year while getting stuff for their

22:26.011 --> 22:26.970
mini-mart.

22:27.054 --> 22:29.097
Mini… mini mart?

22:29.181 --> 22:31.808
Yes, they run a small mini mart.
The Thousand Nyang Department Store.

22:31.892 --> 22:35.354
But in our neighborhood, it basically
counts as a general store.

22:36.396 --> 22:40.442
Oh, Th-- Thousand Nyang, Thousand Nyang
Department Store. Nice.

22:40.525 --> 22:41.485
Very nice.

22:42.652 --> 22:45.113
Know what? There aren't that many
things that cost one 1.000 won

22:45.197 --> 22:47.824
in the store. Prices have gone up so
much these days that most things

22:47.908 --> 22:49.034
cost at least 3,000 won.

22:49.117 --> 22:50.118
Ugh, God.

22:50.619 --> 22:54.414
Why would you go around saying stuff
about me that you have no clue about?

22:54.498 --> 22:57.292
I didn't… Well, you said yourself
on the phone that you were the son of a

22:57.376 --> 23:00.337
department store owner--

23:01.088 --> 23:04.257
Oh, so you were just eavesdropping
on my phone call then.

23:05.384 --> 23:07.803
Mr. Baek, I'm offended right now.
And it's not even just today.

23:07.886 --> 23:10.806
Your attitude's been offensive right from
the beginning. Well, I'm not gonna

23:10.889 --> 23:17.854
put up with it. I don't want you as my
manager So you're fired as of--

23:17.938 --> 23:20.524
I'm done with this! And I won't
do this any longer.

23:23.944 --> 23:27.906
D-- did you just throw down the car key?
As manager?

23:27.989 --> 23:30.659
What are managers? Tell me. Are we not
people?

23:30.742 --> 23:32.577
Screw it, I hope you fail at life.

23:39.709 --> 23:42.921
Mr. Baek! You won't get away with this!

23:47.426 --> 23:50.178
Wh-wh- wh- why is he coming back?
Wh-wh-wh- wait. Wait, wait, wait, wait,

23:50.262 --> 23:51.096
wait.

23:52.973 --> 23:54.558
This goes back to the company.

23:58.061 --> 24:02.315
Are you serious? Hey! How am I
supposed to get home?

24:07.696 --> 24:10.782
Once Seo-jun's school documents
are sorted, would you take care

24:10.866 --> 24:12.492
-of him until I get a nanny? And
-Yes, sir.

24:12.576 --> 24:14.035
Also baseball tickets.

24:15.036 --> 24:16.538
Two tickets for this weekend. Okay?

24:16.621 --> 24:17.998
Seo-jun would like that.

24:20.333 --> 24:23.086
Chairman Choi Mun-do, right? I'm
Inspector Lee Han-su from Seobu Police.

24:23.170 --> 24:29.509
I'd like to ask you a few questions about
the death of nurse An Seong-hui.

24:29.593 --> 24:30.719
I'm sorry, death?

24:30.802 --> 24:34.139
I think he's referring to the case
that Cha Se-gye is involved in.

24:36.475 --> 24:39.269
I can't think how I'd be able to
help you. I don't have much contact with

24:39.352 --> 24:40.228
Se-gye.

24:41.480 --> 24:44.024
I'll decide whether you have contact
with him or not. It's a simple

24:44.107 --> 24:46.485
investigation, I'd appreciate your
cooperation.

24:46.568 --> 24:50.322
I have no reason to help you with this
investigation. If you have questions for

24:50.405 --> 24:51.907
me, issue an official summons.

24:54.201 --> 24:55.035
Uh, Mr. Choi.

25:04.127 --> 25:05.962
REFUSED QUESTIONING

25:06.046 --> 25:09.090
Inspector Lee said, Choi Mun-do's initial
response has been to deny knowledge of

25:09.174 --> 25:11.593
the case. He told the inspector
to issue a summons. I wonder if

25:11.676 --> 25:14.095
that's just buying him time to prepare.

25:14.179 --> 25:17.390
That was my intention. I want to see how
that busy bee moves now.

25:17.474 --> 25:18.475
That busy bee?

25:18.558 --> 25:21.520
When Mun-do was at Chail, they weren't
even indicted, despite all the corrupt

25:21.603 --> 25:24.189
bids. That means the cartel is
very tightly knit. So that's where we

25:24.272 --> 25:28.276
start with this. The very foundation of
Choi Mun-do's power, Chail E&amp;C.

25:28.777 --> 25:29.778
INTERNAL POLICE ACCOMPLICE
KEY ACCOMPLICE

25:29.861 --> 25:32.781
I just found out that the police
officer from Seobu Police Station

25:32.864 --> 25:33.698
questioned Cha.

25:33.782 --> 25:37.744
It seems Se-gye is upset with me. I guess
because I humiliated him in front of

25:37.827 --> 25:41.706
his girl. Does he seriously think he can
pressure me with a nobody inspector?

25:41.790 --> 25:45.377
Prepare a press release. "Former Biojei
CEO Cha Se-gye. Not an ousting, but

25:45.460 --> 25:49.297
an escape. Sucked retail investors dry,
sold shares, and walked away with

25:49.381 --> 25:54.344
over one hundred billion won." Use that.

25:56.596 --> 25:57.430
Yes, sir.

25:59.724 --> 26:01.726
Mr. Choi, check the internet right now.

26:05.689 --> 26:08.149
(EXCLUSIVE) THE TRUE FACE
OF CHAIL CHAIRMAN CHOI MUN-DO EXPOSED!

26:08.233 --> 26:12.195
CHAIL CURRENT CHAIRMAN CHOI MUN-DO'S
ALLEGED BRIBERY FOR CONSTRUCTION CONTRACTS

26:13.238 --> 26:16.575
Choi Mun-do's a pro at manipulating
public opinion with rumors. Being on

26:16.658 --> 26:20.036
the receiving end of it messes with
your head more than you think.

26:20.120 --> 26:23.456
We're taking real action to try and
stop Choi Mun-do's key business, the

26:23.540 --> 26:27.419
resort project. We'll use the fact
that he illegally hired thugs to acquire

26:27.502 --> 26:30.589
ACT ON THE PUNISHMENT OF VIOLENCE, ETC.
ARTICLE 2, PARAGRAPH 2

26:30.672 --> 26:33.967
the city of Jusan, which is just ten
kilometers away from the site,

26:34.050 --> 26:37.679
is pushing to build an international
airport. He'll be hit from both sides.

26:37.762 --> 26:41.433
Internally, by investors, and externally,
by the public. The construction

26:41.516 --> 26:42.642
will then come to a halt.

26:42.726 --> 26:45.186
But Choi Mun-do won't just sit there and
take it.

26:45.687 --> 26:49.482
Of course he won't. He'll come after me.
So then it's a matter of who's worse,

26:49.566 --> 26:52.694
him or me? The media won't know who to
attack more.

26:52.777 --> 26:55.238
So how do you plan to get yourself
out of this?

26:56.615 --> 26:58.742
I won't get out of it. Why?

27:01.661 --> 27:02.787
I have nothing to lose.

27:02.871 --> 27:05.832
The heirs to Chail, Korea's top
conglomerate, are embroiled

27:06.541 --> 27:12.380
PUMP AND DUMP VS. BRIBERY
THE FUTURE OF CHAIL TAINTED BY CORRUPTION

27:13.256 --> 27:16.092
accusations of bribery. Criticism of
Chairman Choi Mun-do is also mounting

27:16.176 --> 27:19.679
ACTING CHAIRMAN CHOI MUN-DO,
ALLEGED USE OF HIRED THUGS TO SECURE SITE

27:25.602 --> 27:28.271
Illegal land purchase. All of these
allegations are groundless. If you

27:28.355 --> 27:30.940
suddenly demanded early repayment
based on fake news from an unknown

27:31.024 --> 27:32.025
figure--

27:36.071 --> 27:38.907
I hear they're going to build an airport
next to the site.

27:38.990 --> 27:40.533
Just ten kilometers away.

27:40.617 --> 27:41.743
Oh, that's…

27:42.285 --> 27:45.246
It's a good thing I have connections
at City Hall. Otherwise, I wouldn't have

27:45.330 --> 27:47.415
had a clue until they broke ground.

27:47.499 --> 27:50.293
If they build an airport next to the
resort, noisy planes will be flying

27:50.377 --> 27:53.004
overhead all the time. How's that
gonna work? Who would actually want

27:53.088 --> 27:54.839
to stay there?

27:55.632 --> 27:58.385
As far as I know, the airport's in the
concept stage. Where did you hear

27:58.468 --> 27:59.719
about that?

28:00.220 --> 28:03.723
I looked into it. Turns out the current
mayor of Jusan is running for

28:03.807 --> 28:06.893
re-election, and securing an
international airport is her key

28:06.976 --> 28:08.311
campaign pledge.

28:08.395 --> 28:10.939
The mayor of Jusan?

28:11.523 --> 28:14.484
Yes, the resort project will progress
without hiccups. We'll also put out the

28:14.567 --> 28:17.987
groundbreaking schedule at our fiftieth
anniversary event.

28:18.071 --> 28:20.281
I'll take that as a promise.
After Songjin, you'll support

28:20.365 --> 28:25.078
Jusan City. After all, a resort is
better than an airport.

28:25.161 --> 28:29.207
Her aide said it wasn't a key campaign
pledge until a month ago, however, she

28:29.290 --> 28:31.334
suddenly changed her stance.

28:31.835 --> 28:32.836
It sounds like…

28:34.879 --> 28:36.673
there's been some kind of deal.

28:36.756 --> 28:39.676
Ms. Jang. You talked like you couldn't
handle it, but you're crushing the

28:39.759 --> 28:42.971
biggest three cardio workouts from hell.

28:43.054 --> 28:45.515
I'm in your hands, alright? I'm
building up my fitness 'cause of

28:45.598 --> 28:46.558
what you promised.

28:47.642 --> 28:51.646
Of course. I'll pave the way straight to
the Blue House for you. You won't walk,

28:51.730 --> 28:52.814
you'll fly right in.

28:58.153 --> 29:00.488
Should we try some strength training
next?

29:00.572 --> 29:02.031
Sure. Over here.

29:02.532 --> 29:05.452
Mochang's got some serious pull. It takes
one word from you to get an

29:05.535 --> 29:06.369
airport built.

29:06.453 --> 29:08.663
You're always taking from me.
When are you going to start

29:08.747 --> 29:10.248
-paying me back?
-Come on now.

29:11.875 --> 29:14.711
Once Jusan Airport opens, I know all
your businesses will get spots in the

29:14.794 --> 29:17.046
duty-free stores. Your jewelry
brand, your restaurants, and

29:17.130 --> 29:18.214
your outdoor lines.

29:18.298 --> 29:21.259
There's got to be something I get for it.
I wouldn't do all this work for you

29:21.342 --> 29:22.552
just because I like you.

29:23.803 --> 29:27.974
I like that mindset. I wanna keep
working as partners.

29:30.393 --> 29:32.103
Yeah, sure, let's do that.

29:34.481 --> 29:37.442
Songjin Resort, Chail's flagship project,
has hit a major roadblock. The city

29:37.525 --> 29:40.653
of Jusan, located ten kilometers from the
site, has announced it's plan to attract

29:40.737 --> 29:43.698
an international airport. This raises
serious questions about the suitability

29:43.782 --> 29:46.534
of the location. Analysts say the
project will be extremely difficult to

29:46.618 --> 29:52.081
move forward with unless the design
is overhauled.

29:53.917 --> 29:57.712
CHAIRMAN CHOI MUN-DO IN DIRE STRAITS,
CORRUPTION SCANDAL, PROJECT ROADBLOCK

30:00.548 --> 30:03.051
During his Chail E&amp;C days, Choi
Mun-do, who recently stepped in as

30:03.134 --> 30:06.095
acting chairman for the company, is now
facing his biggest crisis since taking

30:06.179 --> 30:09.682
the job. Some observers are comparing
Choi Mun-do's management woes to

30:15.438 --> 30:18.525
CHAIL UNDER CHOI MUN-DO IN TURMOIL
FOLLOWING OUSTING OF CHA SE-GYE

30:18.608 --> 30:20.360
Why are they dragging me into this?

30:23.696 --> 30:26.407
Is this what they mean by "blowing
your nose without using your hands?"

30:26.491 --> 30:27.534
And when did you butter up Jusan's mayor?

30:27.617 --> 30:30.620
The more insignificant the politician,
the more they want to flip the game with

30:30.703 --> 30:31.538
a shiny badge.

30:31.621 --> 30:35.041
I just gently scratched that itch
for her, and her ambition took off

30:35.124 --> 30:36.167
on its own.

30:36.251 --> 30:38.837
Choi Mun-do has to be fuming this time.

30:39.462 --> 30:43.383
You always reap what you sow. I'm just
collecting on all the bad karma mileage

30:43.466 --> 30:45.468
that asshole has racked up.

30:57.272 --> 30:59.941
Wow, now you're even showing up
unannounced? Really?

31:00.441 --> 31:01.860
You're supposed to be busy.

31:01.943 --> 31:05.780
Why are you sitting around at home? You
should at least watch something. Oh.

31:06.948 --> 31:08.533
You wanna watch something? Hey, move

31:08.616 --> 31:10.493
-out the way!
-Oh, it's Cha Se-gye.

31:10.577 --> 31:11.828
No, it's not.

31:11.911 --> 31:13.997
Huh? Yes, it is. I definitely saw you.

31:14.080 --> 31:14.956
No, you saw wrong.

31:15.039 --> 31:16.958
Hey, I saw it. It was definitely
Cha Se-gye.

31:17.041 --> 31:17.876
No.

31:42.650 --> 31:43.693
-Damn it.
-Damn it.

31:49.991 --> 31:53.036
What a surprise to see you here. What do
you want?

31:53.912 --> 31:57.832
Fine. Well then, why don't we just
get straight to the point.

32:01.210 --> 32:04.088
Yes, Se-gye. It's finally time for us
to properly join forces. As you know,

32:04.172 --> 32:07.050
your grandfather isn't doing okay, plus
the company's now in a really awful

32:07.133 --> 32:09.719
state, obviously you know. At times
like this, I say the family must

32:09.802 --> 32:12.639
all support each other.

32:16.267 --> 32:19.020
Think about it. Why is Chail called
Chail? Because it belongs to the Cha

32:19.103 --> 32:20.605
family. But,

32:22.231 --> 32:25.902
the head of the company is Choi Mun-do.
That's Choil, not Chail. The name

32:25.985 --> 32:28.947
itself is a contradiction, right?

32:29.447 --> 32:31.491
Right. We can't have Choil.

32:31.991 --> 32:33.993
Right? We can't have that, can we?

32:34.869 --> 32:39.415
But since when were we family? Aren't I
just the little thief to you guys?

32:41.584 --> 32:44.337
Se-gye. Fine, I admit it. we actually
haven't been the closest aunts and

32:44.420 --> 32:50.885
nephew. But when have we ever treated
you like that?

32:51.928 --> 32:53.930
Oh, so I'm not a thief.

32:54.430 --> 32:55.306
I'm just a jerk.

32:55.390 --> 32:56.224
Hey!

32:56.307 --> 32:59.352
Just watch your mouth, will you?
We're here to suggest we work together,

32:59.435 --> 33:00.645
especially with father laid up.

33:00.728 --> 33:03.523
At least get the story straight.
You're not here to work together,

33:03.606 --> 33:06.526
you're here to beg. 'Cause teaming up
with an asshole's better than nothing.

33:06.609 --> 33:09.153
Cha Se-gye! How dare you use
that langauge in front of your elders?

33:09.237 --> 33:11.906
This is why I didn't want to come here.
I was willing to overlook your

33:11.990 --> 33:15.618
mistakes because you're family, but your
attitude is rotten to the core!

33:18.663 --> 33:19.956
Who's rotten to the core?

33:25.003 --> 33:28.423
Cha Se-gye, why are you sitting here
listening to that nonsense?

33:28.506 --> 33:30.591
-Oh…
-Just throw them out of here.

33:31.217 --> 33:36.806
What the hell are you doing here? What?
Are you two together now?

33:36.889 --> 33:38.182
What? You know this girl?

33:38.683 --> 33:40.143
How do you two know each other?

33:40.226 --> 33:42.729
You still haven't learned your
lesson after I beat you with taffy?

33:42.812 --> 33:44.022
I guess I went too easy on you.

33:44.105 --> 33:46.357
You got beaten with taffy? Oh, my God,
no.

33:46.441 --> 33:47.442
What? Did you hit her?

33:47.525 --> 33:50.653
What are you saying? She gave me
a one-sided beatdown.

33:50.737 --> 33:53.156
You're not the type to get beaten up by
anyone.

33:53.865 --> 33:54.699
Listen…

33:54.782 --> 33:58.578
Calm down, Cha Se-gye. I didn't get hit a
single time. It's true your aunt's

33:58.661 --> 34:00.788
the one who was completely owned.

34:02.165 --> 34:06.085
That's what I said. I was the
clear victim, not her.

34:06.753 --> 34:10.673
And yet, here you still have the nerve
to come crawling to harass your nephew.

34:12.592 --> 34:16.512
What? What now? What-- What? What are
you doing? Why did you pluck that out?

34:19.307 --> 34:20.141
Oh, crap.

34:21.434 --> 34:24.395
A good beating's the best medicine for
an attitude problem.

34:25.063 --> 34:28.483
You dumb thug, you! Fine. Come at me.
Come at me, come at me. I've got

34:28.566 --> 34:31.360
backup today. Oh. Hey!

34:34.197 --> 34:35.823
Hey, get out!

34:37.700 --> 34:38.534
Jesus…

34:46.501 --> 34:50.463
What is this? You had to defend me from
my own family?

34:50.546 --> 34:54.217
Those aunts of yours. You'd think
they'd help their nephew. Cha Se-gye,

34:54.300 --> 34:57.762
don't worry. I taught them a lesson, so
they'll leave you alone now.

35:02.183 --> 35:06.229
I know, I was so scared. What would I do
without you?

35:07.313 --> 35:08.147
How smooth.

35:10.399 --> 35:13.528
Are you okay? We can't have you
collapsing again. You're warm.

35:13.611 --> 35:17.156
I'm taking you to the hospital right now.

35:18.116 --> 35:21.661
Okay, let's go. Since I'm starting over,
I should introduce myself.

35:21.744 --> 35:22.870
Wait, what do you mean?

35:22.954 --> 35:25.248
Let's go visit your grandfather together.

35:28.417 --> 35:30.837
How are you feeling? The doctor
says you're recovering, but you

35:30.920 --> 35:33.297
still don't have your memory.

35:33.381 --> 35:36.134
I'm sure it will come back soon.
And if it doesn't, so be it. It doesn't

35:36.217 --> 35:39.804
really affect my life anyhow.

35:44.100 --> 35:47.603
You should keep an eye on the chairman.
I think that he might be up to

35:47.687 --> 35:51.357
something shady. And I think he might be
lying about his memory too. The way

35:51.440 --> 35:55.278
the police and the media move together,
I doubt this would be the work of

35:55.361 --> 35:56.362
Cha alone.

35:58.197 --> 36:00.533
As long as you're good, I'm okay with it.

36:00.616 --> 36:02.827
-Just focus on getting better for now.
-Huh?

36:02.910 --> 36:05.538
And stay away from newspapers.

36:13.379 --> 36:17.300
What's the rush? We easily could've just
left it for a while.

36:18.259 --> 36:20.428
You said your grandfather wanted to
see me.

36:21.179 --> 36:23.806
Yeah, but he didn't mean while
he's in the hospital.

36:24.599 --> 36:27.810
You're visiting together? Have you
forgotten already? I told you

36:27.894 --> 36:31.022
not to visit him for the time being.

36:31.772 --> 36:34.692
Yeah, well… I don't ever listen
to others.

36:37.361 --> 36:40.489
If you care about uncle's health, you'd
better not say anything unnecessary.

36:40.573 --> 36:43.951
It won't do him any good to hear about
the troubles at the company.

36:45.536 --> 36:47.622
The elderly can die at the drop of a hat.

36:51.083 --> 36:54.212
Let them in. If he has any decency,
he'll follow.

37:02.595 --> 37:04.305
Wait here. I'll let him know.

37:09.977 --> 37:12.730
I really owe you quite a lot, Ms. Shin.
Whenever I find myself in a jam,

37:12.813 --> 37:17.235
you're there. I hope you have a good
visit.

37:17.318 --> 37:20.488
Hold on. We have to talk.

37:21.447 --> 37:24.450
Are you sure it's okay for us to meet in
private like this? Se-gye's an awfully

37:24.533 --> 37:25.826
jealous guy.

37:26.327 --> 37:29.205
You find this fun? Toying with people?

37:29.830 --> 37:32.708
No one works for fun. This is just a
matter of survival.

37:35.044 --> 37:37.964
I have no hard feelings toward you,
Ms. Shin, so don't hate me. The resorts,

37:38.047 --> 37:42.009
well… that's something I've staked my
life on.

37:42.093 --> 37:45.596
Yes, you don't care about the means
if you can achieve your goal.

37:46.597 --> 37:50.101
I used to know someone like that.
They were just like you.

37:52.353 --> 37:56.565
What happened to this person? Did they
achieve their goal?

37:57.608 --> 38:00.861
He sure did. He ascended to a
blood-stained throne and ruled over

38:00.945 --> 38:05.199
people like livestock, before withering
away all alone.

38:07.285 --> 38:12.456
In history, he's recorded as a wise king.
Victors write history, anyhow.

38:16.669 --> 38:20.089
Would you like me to tell you a
secret about life? Karma, be it good

38:20.172 --> 38:24.260
or bad, always comes back to you.

38:28.097 --> 38:32.101
What goes around, comes around, and your
own reckoning is only just starting.

38:36.605 --> 38:37.732
Is that a threat?

38:40.651 --> 38:43.070
It's a warning that I won't sit idly
by anymore.

38:43.863 --> 38:47.533
Enduring it once was quite enough for me.
In this life, I will protect me

38:47.616 --> 38:52.038
and mine, and I'll do that no
matter what.

38:53.748 --> 38:54.832
A declaration of war.

38:59.086 --> 39:03.758
Guess we'll see whether you can protect
yourselves in all this.

39:06.552 --> 39:09.638
What makes you think you can just show up
unannounced at this hour to make an

39:09.722 --> 39:10.598
introduction?

39:11.265 --> 39:14.310
This is the first time I'm asking this
of you. So please, do it for me this

39:14.393 --> 39:16.062
once and force yourself to smile.

39:21.692 --> 39:22.943
You wait outside.

39:23.027 --> 39:25.363
I won't leave. How do I know what
you'll say to her?

39:25.446 --> 39:26.906
Do as he says, wait outside.

39:32.995 --> 39:34.955
If he spouts nonsense, please come out.

39:35.539 --> 39:37.333
That- that rotten boy.

39:47.593 --> 39:51.222
I don't like you very much. You are
an orphan who has no one to rely on.

39:51.305 --> 39:54.934
You're not the right person for
him. Listen, I'm not changing my mind on

39:55.017 --> 39:55.851
this.

40:02.441 --> 40:05.861
I understand. Because until
recently, I felt the same way.

40:08.280 --> 40:10.950
Although, I can't help it. Now that
I've been given a new life, I just

40:11.033 --> 40:17.957
can't imagine myself without Cha Se-gye.
I never want to let go of his hand now.

40:24.922 --> 40:27.842
You've made up your mind. So then why are
you here?

40:28.759 --> 40:29.635
To inform me?

40:29.718 --> 40:34.974
Yes, I'm here to inform you I'll
make your grandson happy.

40:38.018 --> 40:44.233
And I'll never leave him alone again.
You can trust me.

41:00.416 --> 41:02.460
Sir, Mr. Choi is here for you.

41:04.837 --> 41:08.591
The case was suddenly transferred to
Seobu Station. Said it came from above,

41:08.674 --> 41:11.218
but I don't think it came from the
captain.

41:11.302 --> 41:14.805
I'm sure it'll come back eventually.
And if it doesn't, then so be it.

41:15.306 --> 41:16.140
Interesting.

41:16.223 --> 41:19.143
Now, I think it'll be hard to
bury this if the investigation goes any

41:19.226 --> 41:21.854
further. In the worst case, it could
even lead to charges. You should

41:21.937 --> 41:23.606
start cleaning things up I think.

41:29.403 --> 41:33.157
You're right. Some cleanup is definitely
needed.

41:42.708 --> 41:45.044
I will have my revenge!

41:45.127 --> 41:45.961
KINGDOM OF WOMEN 2 (FIRST RUN)

41:46.045 --> 41:46.879
Look at that. The venom in her eyes.

41:46.962 --> 41:48.172
FINALE

41:48.255 --> 41:51.509
Oh, my gosh. I'm petrified she'll
appear in my dreams.

41:51.592 --> 41:52.801
"Petrified?"

41:52.885 --> 41:53.719
You wench!

41:53.802 --> 41:54.762
She's very pretty to me.

41:54.845 --> 41:57.556
Oh, you still recognize your
granddaughter? Even as you're losing it,

41:57.640 --> 42:00.893
you're still blinded by love. She looks
like an angel in your eyes.

42:00.976 --> 42:02.144
I'm here to frighten you.

42:02.228 --> 42:03.729
Gosh, when did you get here?

42:04.313 --> 42:06.899
The granddaughter's here. In real
life, you look like an angel.

42:06.982 --> 42:07.816
Oh, I do?

42:07.900 --> 42:09.276
-Yes.
-I'm not venomous now?

42:09.360 --> 42:12.196
I will rip you apart to death!

42:13.531 --> 42:16.242
Let's wait and see, Your Majesty.

42:32.341 --> 42:33.175
Grandma.

42:35.469 --> 42:38.722
What are you staring at? Something there?

42:39.765 --> 42:42.101
The stop. Bus stop.

42:48.816 --> 42:52.820
Where are you in such a hurry to
go? I just got here.

42:55.030 --> 43:00.160
And I have a lot to share with you.
Why do you keep talkiing about the bus?

43:04.790 --> 43:06.750
Your granddaughter's here. Speak to me.

43:09.628 --> 43:10.963
Why can't you look at me?

43:32.610 --> 43:33.444
What's this?

43:33.527 --> 43:36.614
A glamping date. What do you think?
Isn't it awesome? I mean, this thing's

43:36.697 --> 43:38.198
essentially a house on wheels.

43:38.282 --> 43:40.492
Why put a house on wheels? Evacuation?

43:41.368 --> 43:43.829
Why would we evacuate? This isn't
the Korean War.

43:46.457 --> 43:48.083
Do you want to stargaze with me.

43:53.922 --> 43:57.760
You can't ever find stars when you're in
Seoul. You'd have to go at least as far

43:57.843 --> 43:59.011
as Gangneung or Sokcho.

43:59.803 --> 44:03.098
Why go all the way there? This yard
here is absolutely perfect.

44:06.185 --> 44:08.395
Perfect? What, the view of those
apartments?

44:09.355 --> 44:12.107
The warmth of the fire here reminds
me of my childhood. One day, a tiger

44:12.191 --> 44:18.322
appeared, and I ran away. I almost
fell into a lake and perished.

44:18.405 --> 44:21.742
Dang, is… is this really the time
for that?

44:21.825 --> 44:24.119
I meant this is the opposite of
that time.

44:26.163 --> 44:29.124
The fire is warm, you're beside me.

44:33.045 --> 44:33.879
Man…

44:45.015 --> 44:48.394
After that wild detour through that
time and finally arriving here,

44:48.477 --> 44:52.147
it's like I've woken from a dream.
I still can't quite grasp it, that I'm

44:52.231 --> 44:55.943
back here. It's my home again.

44:59.822 --> 45:03.450
If you can't believe it, think how
I feel. I dream about it every night.

45:04.535 --> 45:06.495
Do you still have dreams about it?

45:08.247 --> 45:12.751
Let's not. What a dumbass. I'm
totally not like him.

45:14.253 --> 45:17.673
Of course not. You're a different
pereson. You were the first one to

45:17.756 --> 45:20.759
look at me with kindness and fill up
my heart.

45:24.430 --> 45:28.434
When I think of you. I feel like
I could fly…

45:30.602 --> 45:32.438
but then I get scared I'll lose you.

45:34.523 --> 45:36.024
My heart goes back and forth…

45:36.734 --> 45:38.026
dozens of times a day.

45:40.446 --> 45:42.030
But I don't really care at all.

45:45.200 --> 45:46.535
Is love often like that?

45:48.787 --> 45:50.748
Is this what people mean when…

45:53.584 --> 45:54.960
they refer to love?

46:00.466 --> 46:04.178
Hey, why did you have to beat me to it?
The man should be the first one to

46:04.261 --> 46:05.179
say that.

46:05.262 --> 46:07.514
What a boomer thing to say. Who cares?

46:08.015 --> 46:12.019
I want… a do-over. I'm gonna splurge and
then make the most romantic--

46:16.064 --> 46:19.818
You're gonna keep on do-- And coming
over here without--

46:21.945 --> 46:22.780
Kissing me whe--

46:24.573 --> 46:28.494
I'll keep doing it. If you save it up,
it turns to crap. Didn't I say that?

46:49.515 --> 46:55.229
Stop it already, would you? Just stop it.
Take it inside. If you're gonna sit

46:55.312 --> 46:58.816
-out here and rub it in, do it inside.
-Let's… Can I stay over?

47:03.445 --> 47:04.863
How did we rub it in?

47:09.618 --> 47:11.245
He showed up out of nowhere…

47:13.539 --> 47:16.041
so I guess I have to come in. I have
no choice.

47:21.255 --> 47:22.673
Did you turn off the boiler?

47:27.928 --> 47:30.848
Is it broken? You're sleeping this way?

47:30.931 --> 47:32.307
What? What's wrong?

47:32.391 --> 47:35.769
You could freeze to death in here.
It's even colder than out there.

47:35.853 --> 47:37.980
This is practically a balmy spring day.
When I stayed in the mountains,

47:38.063 --> 47:40.858
I thought my nose would fall off from
the freezing cold.

47:40.941 --> 47:42.359
Ugh, enough of that talk.

47:43.193 --> 47:46.363
-We're going to my place.
-What? No, we can't. We've been drinking.

47:46.446 --> 47:47.281
Ah…

47:49.533 --> 47:53.579
See, you shouldn't have downed
drinks like that.

48:04.798 --> 48:07.676
Cha Se-gye, come in here. Let's share
a blanket.

48:10.596 --> 48:11.680
I'm not that cold.

48:14.182 --> 48:15.559
I actually run pretty hot.

48:18.061 --> 48:18.896
Always have.

48:20.397 --> 48:22.941
Whatever. Your nose is red, you know.

48:28.614 --> 48:29.948
Hey you, freeze right now.

48:31.491 --> 48:33.535
-Huh?
-Hands up, right now. Come on.

48:53.013 --> 48:54.932
How's this? You like it?

48:55.015 --> 48:58.477
Who suggests hugging by… by yelling,
freeze?

48:59.061 --> 49:01.688
I said it because your face looks like a
criminal.

49:44.398 --> 49:45.232
What?

49:46.858 --> 49:47.693
It's nothing.

49:49.528 --> 49:53.031
Work's been rough lately, right?
Why don't you take a break? Go off on

49:53.115 --> 49:54.324
a trip or something?

49:55.701 --> 49:56.576
A trip?

49:57.828 --> 50:02.416
Go abroad for a little bit breathe
some fresh air. Think of it as a bonus.

50:08.714 --> 50:11.675
Starting tomorrow, guard the chairman's
hospital suite. You don't have to

50:11.758 --> 50:12.968
pick up Seo-jun anymore.

50:16.638 --> 50:19.182
SONGJIN GENERAL HOSPITAL

50:30.193 --> 50:31.903
She must be at the bus stop again.

50:34.781 --> 50:36.491
Should I have gotten a bigger one?

50:42.122 --> 50:45.292
You're here. I was just about to
call you.

50:45.375 --> 50:46.960
Is my grandma at the bus stop now?

50:47.044 --> 50:49.671
Her condition suddenly took a turn
for the worse. She's been moved to

50:49.755 --> 50:50.756
the ICU.

50:59.139 --> 51:02.309
She had a seizure, so we moved her
to the ICU. We've gotten her through

51:02.392 --> 51:05.854
the worst with medication. She's been
holding on for a long time now.

51:17.532 --> 51:21.119
Listen to me very carefully. In life,
there will be storms with thunder

51:21.203 --> 51:24.539
and lightning. When it comes, an
umbrella won't be enough for her.

51:24.623 --> 51:28.585
Just stand and get wet with her.

51:36.468 --> 51:41.640
You can endure a lot of things, if
you're not alone. Having someone helps.

51:43.934 --> 51:47.187
So… can I trust you'll be there?
No matter what happens, you must

51:47.270 --> 51:48.772
protect her.

51:53.693 --> 51:55.195
You can't even die before her!

52:03.328 --> 52:04.162
Yes.

52:15.757 --> 52:16.591
Yes,

52:18.760 --> 52:21.847
I'll protect her. I will.

52:31.398 --> 52:33.900
Go get some sleep. I'll stay here.

52:35.777 --> 52:40.115
No, I don't know when she'll wake up.
You should go.

52:40.615 --> 52:42.284
I can't leave you here alone.

52:45.328 --> 52:48.415
Wait here. I'll go get you some
clothes and something to eat.

53:11.229 --> 53:16.484
Grandma. Grandma, are you awake? Are you
all right?

53:19.446 --> 53:23.575
Should I… get the doctor? The doctor…

53:29.080 --> 53:31.082
Bus… The bus s--

53:37.297 --> 53:39.007
-What, Grandma?
-stop…

53:40.258 --> 53:44.763
B-- bus stop? Y-- you wanna go to the
bus stop?

53:44.846 --> 53:45.972
Where is…

53:47.849 --> 53:49.684
the bus headed?

53:50.852 --> 53:53.063
Where am I headed?

53:55.857 --> 53:59.194
Why are you saying you're going
somewhere? You can't go right now,

53:59.277 --> 54:03.448
there's… There's no time, there's…
grandma.

54:04.115 --> 54:06.284
Where am I headed?

54:06.368 --> 54:07.327
Grandma.

54:09.496 --> 54:14.000
Come on. Come on. No, wait, wait, wait.
Wait.

54:16.544 --> 54:18.630
Grandma. Grandma?

54:22.550 --> 54:27.305
Grandma, where you're headed will…
Grandma, where you're headed will be…

54:56.459 --> 54:58.253
Grandma, you look good today.

54:58.336 --> 55:00.797
Yes, I'm feeling great right now.

55:01.881 --> 55:03.174
Wanna make a run for it?

55:03.883 --> 55:05.135
Run away? Now?

55:05.635 --> 55:07.804
Quickly, now. Let's go.

55:13.351 --> 55:15.103
-Where's her guardian?
-What is it?

55:15.729 --> 55:18.023
-Goodness. Ms. Nam!
-Huh?

55:18.106 --> 55:19.691
We'll sneak out of your room.

55:20.608 --> 55:21.443
After them!

55:22.861 --> 55:25.030
-Ugh.
-Oh, oh, Ms. Nam.

55:25.113 --> 55:26.239
Ms. Shin!

55:30.118 --> 55:31.536
People are running after us.

55:32.454 --> 55:34.664
-Ms. Nam.
-But we managed to shake them off.

55:35.206 --> 55:36.041
Damn.

55:38.251 --> 55:40.503
-Hey, Ms. Nam!
-Where are they?

55:42.005 --> 55:42.839
Ms. Nam.

55:45.258 --> 55:46.176
Let's go.

55:46.259 --> 55:48.219
Let's go. No one can stop us.

55:57.979 --> 56:01.358
At the bus stop, the bus is waiting
for us.

56:08.782 --> 56:11.159
You get in the driver's seat, and we
take off.

56:12.452 --> 56:13.286
Let's go.

56:43.608 --> 56:49.739
Oh, this is great. The sky is clear,
and I have you with me.

56:51.241 --> 56:54.494
We drive along the mountain roads,
passing all the other cars. As we

56:54.577 --> 56:59.207
speed along, the wind blows past us.

57:08.591 --> 57:11.845
Every time we pull up at a bus
stop, people cheer for us, as they

57:11.928 --> 57:14.139
applaud and smile.

57:25.817 --> 57:26.776
All aboard.

57:26.860 --> 57:28.528
-Hey, wait a minute.
-Come on in.

57:28.611 --> 57:30.280
-Where are we going,
-Ms. Nam.

57:30.363 --> 57:32.031
It's been awhile since I saw you.

57:32.740 --> 57:34.617
Aw, thank you so much.

57:34.701 --> 57:35.743
How are you doing?

57:35.827 --> 57:36.828
Hello, hi.

57:37.537 --> 57:39.456
Ms. Nam, where are we going today?

57:39.539 --> 57:40.498
Somewhere nice.

57:41.916 --> 57:42.917
Let's roll!

57:43.668 --> 57:45.545
All right, everybody.

57:45.628 --> 57:47.297
Yes, let's go.

57:48.381 --> 57:50.216
-We're off! We're off! Yay!
-Let's go, let's go.

57:50.300 --> 57:52.343
-All right!
-Here we go!

57:53.511 --> 57:56.055
This is gonna be so great! Yeah!
Let's sing.

57:56.139 --> 57:57.348
Yeah, yeah, let's all sing!

57:57.432 --> 57:59.058
One, two, three, four.

57:59.142 --> 58:02.103
The day when the sun shines brightly
will return. The day when the sun shines

58:02.187 --> 58:03.354
brightly will return. I'm here.

58:03.438 --> 58:06.399
The day when the sun shines brightly
will return. The day when the sun shines

58:06.483 --> 58:07.650
brightly will return. I'm here.

58:07.734 --> 58:08.568
Hey!

58:09.903 --> 58:10.737
Hey!

58:10.820 --> 58:13.656
Forget all your sadness and loneliness.
Nothing is impossible if you try.

58:13.740 --> 58:16.409
The day when the sun shines brightly
will return. The day when the sun

58:16.493 --> 58:18.244
-shines brightly will return.
-Hey!

58:21.539 --> 58:22.790
All right!

58:24.959 --> 58:26.961
And so everyone…

58:30.757 --> 58:32.467
happily rides together.

58:35.512 --> 58:36.513
Happily?

58:39.516 --> 58:41.142
Yes. happily.

58:43.853 --> 58:44.938
And then we…

58:47.732 --> 58:52.320
keep on driving until we reach the
end of the world.

58:58.993 --> 59:01.996
There are no tears or sadness there.

59:03.998 --> 59:05.917
Everyone blesses you with a smile.

59:09.879 --> 59:12.715
They praise you for doing a great job.

59:15.426 --> 59:17.345
They tell you this life was a success.

59:18.596 --> 59:19.472
Of course…

59:21.933 --> 59:27.647
it was a success. With this life, I was
lucky.

59:57.218 --> 59:59.095
And that's the way you go back…

01:00:01.264 --> 01:00:02.890
to where you came from.

01:00:05.226 --> 01:00:06.519
To how you looked before.

01:00:09.230 --> 01:00:10.898
Happily, with a big smile.

01:01:00.198 --> 01:01:03.910
You're here, my angel is here.

01:01:10.124 --> 01:01:11.125
Grandma!

01:02:04.303 --> 01:02:05.263
Grandma.

01:02:13.146 --> 01:02:13.980
Grandma.

01:02:15.940 --> 01:02:18.025
Grandma. Grandma…

01:02:24.365 --> 01:02:28.453
Seo-ri's here. Seo-ri's here now.

01:02:37.503 --> 01:02:38.421
Grandma…

01:02:41.257 --> 01:02:42.425
Seo-ri's here now.

01:03:04.405 --> 01:03:05.990
-Mom. Mom!
-Hi! How was school?

01:03:06.574 --> 01:03:07.408
Okay.

01:03:08.785 --> 01:03:10.495
-Thank you.
-No, no, it was the-- It's on me.

01:03:10.578 --> 01:03:11.412
Hello. Okay, bye.

01:03:11.496 --> 01:03:13.998
-I can't wait. See you later.
-It's okay, I don't mind.

01:03:14.081 --> 01:03:15.291
Your nanny's a bit busy, that's why
I'm here.

01:03:15.374 --> 01:03:16.209
Okay.

01:03:24.425 --> 01:03:26.511
Where is he? Is he in bed?

01:03:26.594 --> 01:03:29.013
Um, he's not home at the moment.

01:03:29.096 --> 01:03:30.056
What do you mean?

01:03:30.139 --> 01:03:33.017
The nanny said your chauffeur picked him
up.

01:03:37.188 --> 01:03:40.441
Get all the CCTV footage around the
school and track all his movements.

01:03:40.525 --> 01:03:42.401
Search anywhere Seo-jun could've gone

01:03:49.242 --> 01:03:50.618
SECRETARY SEO
INCOMING CALL

01:03:54.580 --> 01:03:55.540
Where have you been?

01:03:55.623 --> 01:03:57.416
At the hospital with the chairman.

01:03:57.500 --> 01:03:59.043
Why are you there? Why?

01:04:00.086 --> 01:04:02.630
The chairman wanted to see Seo-jun.

01:04:27.488 --> 01:04:30.658
Uncle, what are you doing?

01:04:31.409 --> 01:04:35.204
What? It it wrong for a grandfather to
want to see his grandson? You should've

01:04:35.288 --> 01:04:38.332
brought him to see me sooner.
If it weren't for Seo, I wouldn't

01:04:38.416 --> 01:04:40.126
even have known he was here.

01:04:40.209 --> 01:04:44.463
Are you threatening me by taking Seo-jun?
Why are you going this far?

01:04:44.964 --> 01:04:48.384
Yes. I always knew you were rotten
inside, but I didn't know the

01:04:48.467 --> 01:04:52.054
full extent of it. I shot myself in
the foot by having faith in a beast

01:04:52.138 --> 01:04:55.558
like you. You're not even human, so why
should I treat you like one?

01:04:55.641 --> 01:04:59.604
Even animals cherish their own offspring.
Can't you see, a child is precious to

01:04:59.687 --> 01:05:01.439
their parents?

01:05:08.821 --> 01:05:11.908
Why do you keep harassing a kid who
grew up without his dad's love?

01:05:11.991 --> 01:05:14.160
There's a limit to how much I
can tolerate!

01:05:16.078 --> 01:05:19.707
If that's all true, you should've
taken better care of him from the start.

01:05:19.790 --> 01:05:22.293
The scars you get as a boy last
a lifetime.

01:05:46.651 --> 01:05:50.071
Nothing hurts so much as when your
child falls over. I felt like all

01:05:50.154 --> 01:05:52.990
the blood was draining from my body
earlier.

01:05:53.824 --> 01:05:56.827
If you hate me, you should've
come for me. Why'd you have to

01:05:56.911 --> 01:05:58.496
involve my child.

01:06:06.379 --> 01:06:07.213
You've issued…

01:06:09.090 --> 01:06:12.760
a real threat. And you've crossed a
line you shouldn't have. From now on,

01:06:12.843 --> 01:06:14.929
everything you have coming is on you.

01:06:17.932 --> 01:06:18.891
Accept that.

01:06:54.218 --> 01:06:55.302
She never wore them.

01:06:58.514 --> 01:07:00.975
She saved them and they're not even that
special.

01:07:16.449 --> 01:07:18.117
I wish she hadn't.

01:07:26.834 --> 01:07:28.502
Are you sure you wanna stay here?

01:07:36.844 --> 01:07:39.680
You haven't gotten any sleep yet or had
anything to eat.

01:07:45.269 --> 01:07:48.856
If you're not hungry, at least have some
fruit. Wait here.

01:07:57.073 --> 01:07:59.992
It looks like just an ordinary
painting, but in reality it

01:08:00.076 --> 01:08:03.829
actually holds two secrets. Because in
Joseon times, it was rare to paint a

01:08:03.913 --> 01:08:07.500
woman's face due to Confucian values
that kept men and women apart. And

01:08:07.583 --> 01:08:13.923
that means this was painted in secret by
her lover.

01:08:15.424 --> 01:08:17.259
That painting of the lady is intersting.

01:08:17.343 --> 01:08:20.137
There was also a rumor about this
painting. Can anyone guess what it was?

01:08:20.221 --> 01:08:22.515
It looks like something stopped it
from burning all the way.

01:08:22.598 --> 01:08:24.225
-Seems mysterious.
-What was it?

01:08:24.308 --> 01:08:26.435
-Can you explain what the curator's
-And in fact, there was quite the

01:08:26.519 --> 01:08:27.937
-saying?
-scandalous rumor about him.

01:08:28.020 --> 01:08:30.981
There are bad rumors about the owner of
the painting. Like…

01:08:32.233 --> 01:08:34.568
-ghosts,
-Isn't that fascinating? So interesting.

01:08:34.652 --> 01:08:36.403
Spirits, and goblins.

01:08:37.446 --> 01:08:43.577
Interesting. So what happened? How does
the story end? Is it a happy ending?

01:08:50.626 --> 01:08:54.463
Since the yaksha fell in love, there was
no way the story could have a happy

01:08:54.547 --> 01:08:56.215
ending. It was a sad ending.

01:09:09.186 --> 01:09:12.565
But apparently, the two lovers from
300 years ago, whose love was never

01:09:12.648 --> 01:09:16.443
fulfilled, are going to meet again soon,
as if by fate.

01:09:17.903 --> 01:09:21.073
Silent night, holy night. Today is
Christmas Eve. The last night we

01:09:21.157 --> 01:09:25.870
can see the Star of the Temptress
from Earth has finally come.

01:09:27.163 --> 01:09:29.498
Are we finally going to be done with
all this?

01:09:30.958 --> 01:09:34.461
The wor-- last-- lea-- bittersw--

01:09:43.470 --> 01:09:48.726
Ow, it's just-- Oh, no, please. No, no,
please.

01:10:02.281 --> 01:10:05.242
Your Highness, pray, come back.

01:10:07.745 --> 01:10:11.123
Silent night, holy night. Today is
Christmas Eve. The last night we

01:10:11.207 --> 01:10:14.793
can see the Star of the Temptress
from Earth has finally come. The word

01:10:14.877 --> 01:10:18.130
"last" always leaves something of
a bittersweet feeling. It seems

01:10:18.214 --> 01:10:25.012
the Star of the Temptress also intends
to leave us with a meaningful farewell.

01:10:41.028 --> 01:10:41.862
Appreciate it.

01:10:41.946 --> 01:10:44.949
Tonight in the night sky, they say a
meteor shower will accompany the path of

01:10:45.032 --> 01:10:47.743
the disappearing comet. How about
we join in for a moment on this final

01:10:47.826 --> 01:10:49.828
journey of the stars as they rain
down like a shower?

01:10:49.912 --> 01:10:50.746
-Hello.
-Hi.

01:10:53.749 --> 01:10:58.379
Could this become a truly special
Christmas Eve we'll never forget?

01:11:03.509 --> 01:11:04.343
Excuse me.

01:12:47.279 --> 01:12:48.614
She'll be waiting for me.

01:13:12.054 --> 01:13:14.431
Your Highness, pray, come back.

01:13:34.368 --> 01:13:39.623
Please, don't die. Don't die, Cha Se-gye.
Don't die. Don't die, Cha Se-gye!

01:13:40.165 --> 01:13:43.293
Blood pressure's still dropping.
85 over 55. Pulse, 130. Ma'am

01:13:43.377 --> 01:13:44.878
please wait!

01:13:54.138 --> 01:13:55.639
Stay calm. Sir, sir!

01:13:55.722 --> 01:13:58.475
Blood pressure's still dropping.
Heart rate, 120. He's gone into cardiac

01:13:58.559 --> 01:14:00.269
-arrest.
-CPR.

01:14:05.566 --> 01:14:07.317
He will not die…

01:14:09.361 --> 01:14:10.195
Your Highness.

01:14:16.618 --> 01:14:17.453
You are…

01:14:19.371 --> 01:14:20.372
not Fortune Teller Geum.

01:14:20.456 --> 01:14:21.832
Do not worry.

01:14:22.791 --> 01:14:28.338
You can save him if you sever the
cycle of fate.

01:14:29.214 --> 01:14:30.340
"The cycle of fate?"

01:14:33.218 --> 01:14:37.055
Your lover will always meet his death,
whether in Joseon or here. So go back

01:14:37.139 --> 01:14:44.062
and save the Grand Prince, for fate
will not repeat itself.

01:14:48.358 --> 01:14:52.279
All you need is to pay a small price.

01:14:54.364 --> 01:14:58.702
Tell me. What is the price? I'll pay!
Whatever the cost, I'll pay it!

01:14:59.203 --> 01:15:02.372
Even if it means that you can never come
back here?

01:15:04.291 --> 01:15:05.667
Never come back here?

01:15:05.751 --> 01:15:11.465
Yes. You will not be able to return
ever again.

01:15:15.052 --> 01:15:16.470
It really is shining…

01:15:18.805 --> 01:15:19.932
now that I"m with you.

01:15:25.187 --> 01:15:26.855
You're the only one, Shin Seo-ri.

01:15:27.981 --> 01:15:32.778
I will not let you be alone. You can
trust me.

01:15:38.700 --> 01:15:42.454
Cha Se-gye, let's grow old together
and never part.

01:15:46.792 --> 01:15:50.295
MY ROYAL NEMESIS

01:16:20.450 --> 01:16:24.162
You can save him if you sever the
cycle of fate.

01:16:24.246 --> 01:16:26.039
I'm back in Joseon.

01:16:26.707 --> 01:16:28.667
You used to serve at Hyeon's quarters,
did you not?

01:16:28.750 --> 01:16:31.670
Do you mean to say you are sending me
to the Grand Prince? He's still alive.

01:16:31.753 --> 01:16:33.630
I can save him.

01:16:34.256 --> 01:16:37.467
Do not drink it. It is poison. He is
trying to use me as bait.

01:16:37.551 --> 01:16:39.177
What do you think you are to me?

01:16:40.429 --> 01:16:41.305
Where's Shin Seo-ri?

01:16:41.388 --> 01:16:43.765
Why, can't you find her? Maybe she's
run away.

01:16:44.683 --> 01:16:49.563
Could you not make me wait any longer?
I can't breathe, Shin Seo-ri.

01:16:50.397 --> 01:16:53.734
This time. I will save you.
